        "original_id": "a2105606-8a86-5c85-aa99-7fb1a285e934",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Auty, Mary Plazas, Giacomo Puccini\n- Works: La Bohème (2009 film), La bohème, \"O soave fanciulla\", \"Walking in the Air\"\n- Places: Ethiopia, Britain, continental Europe\n- Organizations: St Paul's Cathedral, Stiff Records, major opera companies\n- Roles: English operatic tenor, choirboy\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Robert Auty was born on 4 November 1969 and is an English operatic tenor.\n- Peter Auty has worked with most of the major opera companies in Britain and with a number of companies in continental Europe.\n- In the film \"Walking in the Air,\" the song was performed by St Paul's Cathedral choirboy Peter Auty and was reissued in 1985 on Stiff Records and again in 1987.\n- The 2009 film \"La Bohème\" is four minutes long and features images of harsh life in Ethiopia.\n- The 2009 film \"La Bohème\" is set to the duet \"O soave fanciulla\" from Giacomo Puccini's opera \"La bohème,\" sung by Peter Auty and Mary Plazas.",
